    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "I was there is I had more to do with passing that bill than Joe Biden did. All he did was sign it. And this has been the biggest bridge project. in Kentucky for 25 years, huge, huge issue in our state. And I saw a way to put together a bipartisan group in the Senate that could actually pass the bill. I enabled it. It happened. And look, I got elected by the people of Kentucky and I don't view my job, even though I'm the Republican leader of the Senate. is objecting to everything just because Joe Biden might sign the bill. And so that's why I was there. He had the easy part. He just got to sign the bill. I had the hard part. I had to put it together.",
