    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. I mean, both of them are examples of people who were involved in some of the bipartisan agreements that we reached. The biggest one was on infrastructure. And look, obviously, I'm a partisan. I'm the leader of my party in the Senate. But I think no matter who gets elected, American people look at us and say, okay, you have big differences, but surely you can find some things you could agree on and do those. And that was an example of something that we could find agreement on that we needed to do. The two previous national administrations had taken a shot at it unsuccessfully. I thought it was time to put this problem in the end zone and we did.",
