    "turn_idx": 47,
    "turn_text": "Well, look, the end is when Russia loses. And the reason that's extremely important is because the cost of this if Russia wins is only just beginning. Now, the Ukrainians are doing the fighting. We're doing the supplying along with our European allies, NATO allies. If the Russians were to actually win, the cost would be astronomical. So if you look at it that way, the 40 billion or so we've sent the Ukraine in so far and equipment is a pittance compared to the impact of Russian success. This also has a big impact on the Far East. The Prime Minister of Japan said if you want to deter a President Xi of China, beat Putin and Ukraine, because Xi is also looking at this, and thinking whether or not he might be able to take Taiwan, which would have an enormous impact on the world economy, because Taiwan is a thriving, prosperous, island, quasi-nation, deeply involved in international trade. And at the moment, the biggest supplier of microchips in the entire world. So look, you can pay me now or pay me later. Remember that old commercial? Believe me, for those who doubt about what we're doing in Ukraine, we're doing the right thing. And in fact, my criticism of the President, he hadn't done it quite soon enough. And we need to stick with the Ukrainians. They can win this war and they need to win this war.",
