    "turn_idx": 94,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think at the state level, many states are moving in the direction of taxing consumption instead of income. Tennessee, for example, Florida, for example, Texas, for example, have no income tax. They were allowing other kinds of taxes. And Kentucky, because I'm sure you've talked about on this program, is trying to move in the direction of different revenue sources. Now, why would they do that? It turns out... that companies that are locating have a lot of interest in the tax structure in making decisions to locate. There were two ways in which we always had trouble competing with Tennessee. Tennessee was right to work and we were not. This new Republican legislature cured that. We now have a right to work state. The second problem was Tennessee had no income tax and we did.",
